            <ArticleTitle>The clustered needling, massage and cupping used for treatment of obstinate myofascitis of the back--a report of 68 cases.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>113-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The clustered needling, massage and cupping have been used together for treatment of myofascitis of the back with good therapeutic results through the joint effects of removing blood stasis, promoting blood circulation, dredging the channels, promoting themetabolism and the repair of the tissues, impairing and relaxing the affected muscles.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
